{"source": "component.go", "source_sha256": "ba84f0c6f80d488371cba44f100c10906a937423f754d5db24053ce52e13c4e1", "draft": {"model": "deepseek-flash", "finish_reason": "stop", "input_tokens": 620, "output_tokens": 1563, "cost_microdollars": 2062, "reservation_microdollars": 15394}, "verification": {"model": "jev-1.14.0", "input_tokens": 3003, "cost_microdollars": 127, "reservation_microdollars": 526, "error": null}, "claims": {"C1": {"kind": "claim", "statement": "A() increments the Target's Requests count at call time, before returning the closure.", "line": 8, "fragment": "p.Target.Requests++", "citation_check": "ok", "jev": {"choice": "supported", "probabilities": {"supported": 0.89, "contradicted": 0.0, "unclear": 0.11}, "confidence": 0.83}}, "C2": {"kind": "claim", "statement": "A() captures the Target's Epoch value at call time into a local variable.", "line": 9, "fragment": "epoch := p.Target.Epoch", "citation_check": "ok", "jev": {"choice": "supported", "probabilities": {"supported": 0.99, "contradicted": 0.0, "unclear": 0.01}, "confidence": 0.98}}, "C3": {"kind": "claim", "statement": "The closure returned by A() increments Successes only if the Target's current Epoch equals the captured epoch.", "line": 10, "fragment": "if p.Target.Epoch == epoch { p.Target.Successes++ }", "citation_check": "ok", "jev": {"choice": "supported", "probabilities": {"supported": 1.0, "contradicted": 0.0, "unclear": 0.0}, "confidence": 1.0}}, "C4": {"kind": "claim", "statement": "B() captures the Target pointer into a local variable and increments that target's Requests.", "line": 13, "fragment": "target := p.Target", "citation_check": "ok", "jev": {"choice": "supported", "probabilities": {"supported": 0.73, "contradicted": 0.01, "unclear": 0.26}, "confidence": 0.6}}, "C5": {"kind": "claim", "statement": "B() increments the captured target's Requests at call time.", "line": 14, "fragment": "target.Requests++", "citation_check": "ok", "jev": {"choice": "supported", "probabilities": {"supported": 0.93, "contradicted": 0.0, "unclear": 0.07}, "confidence": 0.89}}, "C6": {"kind": "claim", "statement": "The closure returned by B() unconditionally increments the captured target's Successes.", "line": 15, "fragment": "target.Successes++", "citation_check": "ok", "jev": {"choice": "supported", "probabilities": {"supported": 0.99, "contradicted": 0.0, "unclear": 0.01}, "confidence": 0.98}}, "C7": {"kind": "claim", "statement": "C() captures both the Target pointer and its Epoch at call time into local variables.", "line": 18, "fragment": "target, epoch := p.Target, p.Target.Epoch", "citation_check": "ok", "jev": {"choice": "supported", "probabilities": {"supported": 1.0, "contradicted": 0.0, "unclear": 0.0}, "confidence": 1.0}}, "C8": {"kind": "claim", "statement": "C() increments the captured target's Requests at call time.", "line": 19, "fragment": "target.Requests++", "citation_check": "ok", "jev": {"choice": "supported", "probabilities": {"supported": 0.92, "contradicted": 0.01, "unclear": 0.07}, "confidence": 0.88}}, "C9": {"kind": "claim", "statement": "The closure returned by C() increments Successes only if p.Target still equals the captured target and the target's Epoch equals the captured epoch.", "line": 20, "fragment": "if p.Target == target && target.Epoch == epoch { target.Successes++ }", "citation_check": "ok", "jev": {"choice": "supported", "probabilities": {"supported": 1.0, "contradicted": 0.0, "unclear": 0.0}, "confidence": 1.0}}, "C10": {"kind": "claim", "statement": "D() increments Requests on the entry currently mapped to key at call time.", "line": 23, "fragment": "r.Entries[key].Requests++", "citation_check": "ok", "jev": {"choice": "supported", "probabilities": {"supported": 0.96, "contradicted": 0.0, "unclear": 0.04}, "confidence": 0.94}}, "C11": {"kind": "claim", "statement": "The closure returned by D() looks up the key again at invocation time and increments Successes only if the looked-up entry is not nil.", "line": 24, "fragment": "if target := r.Entries[key]; target != nil { target.Successes++ }", "citation_check": "ok", "jev": {"choice": "supported", "probabilities": {"supported": 1.0, "contradicted": 0.0, "unclear": 0.0}, "confidence": 1.0}}, "C12": {"kind": "claim", "statement": "E() has a value receiver, so it operates on a copy of the Port; it increments the Target's Requests at call time.", "line": 27, "fragment": "p.Target.Requests++", "citation_check": "ok", "jev": {"choice": "unclear", "probabilities": {"supported": 0.48, "contradicted": 0.03, "unclear": 0.49}, "confidence": 0.24}}, "C13": {"kind": "claim", "statement": "The closure returned by E() unconditionally increments the copy's Target's Successes; the copy's Target field is fixed to the value captured in the receiver copy.", "line": 28, "fragment": "p.Target.Successes++", "citation_check": "ok", "jev": {"choice": "supported", "probabilities": {"supported": 0.73, "contradicted": 0.02, "unclear": 0.25}, "confidence": 0.6}}, "C14": {"kind": "claim", "statement": "F() captures p.Target into a local variable and increments that target's Requests.", "line": 31, "fragment": "target := p.Target", "citation_check": "ok", "jev": {"choice": "supported", "probabilities": {"supported": 0.72, "contradicted": 0.02, "unclear": 0.26}, "confidence": 0.58}}, "C15": {"kind": "claim", "statement": "F() increments the captured target's Requests at call time.", "line": 32, "fragment": "target.Requests++", "citation_check": "ok", "jev": {"choice": "supported", "probabilities": {"supported": 0.87, "contradicted": 0.01, "unclear": 0.12}, "confidence": 0.8}}, "C16": {"kind": "claim", "statement": "The closure returned by F() unconditionally increments the captured target's Successes.", "line": 33, "fragment": "target.Successes++", "citation_check": "ok", "jev": {"choice": "supported", "probabilities": {"supported": 0.95, "contradicted": 0.0, "unclear": 0.05}, "confidence": 0.92}}}, "questions": ["In A(), is the intended semantic for 'Successes' to count completions only within the same epoch as when the factory was invoked? Line 10 compares p.Target.Epoch but line 9 captures epoch; is there an intended behavior when p.Target itself changes between invocation and completion?", "In C(), line 20 checks both pointer identity (p.Target == target) and epoch equality; line 9/A only checks epoch. Is this asymmetry intentional, and what is the intended behavior for A() when p.Target is reassigned to a different Account?", "In D(), Requests is incremented on r.Entries[key] but if the key is absent or nil at call time, line 23 would be a nil dereference; is nil/absent handling intended and is it specified?", "In D(), the closure re-reads r.Entries[key] at completion, so a map entry replaced between invocation and completion will record Successes on the new entry; is that intended, and how should the correspondence between Requests and Successes be accounted across replacement?", "In E(), the value receiver copies Port, so the closure mutates p.Target.Successes on the captured Target pointer; if the original Port.Target is reassigned meanwhile, the closure still increments the old Target. Is that intended, or should E share the pointer/epoch semantics of A/C?", "In B() and F(), the closures increment Successes unconditionally on the captured target with no epoch or identity check; is it intended that B and F count completions regardless of any later state changes (e.g., Target reassignment or Epoch bump)?", "Lines 8, 14, 19, 23, 27, 32 increment Requests at factory invocation time, while Successes is incremented at completion; is the intended accounting pairing one invocation to one completion, and what should happen if the returned closure is never called (Requests incremented without Successes)?", "Is there any ordering requirement between the increment of Requests (line 8/14/19/23/27/32) and any subsequent mutation of Epoch or Target such that a completion is attributed to invocation-time state? The sources do not state one.", "If the returned closures are invoked concurrently or multiple times, is the intended behavior one Successes increment per call, or one per factory invocation? No source line constrains this.", "Does any behavior ensure p.Target (line 8, 9, 10, 13, 18, 20, 27, 28, 31) is non-nil? No source line checks for nil Target, and the observable behavior under a nil Target is not specified.", "Is the difference in epoch-checking between A (epoch only, line 10) and C (identity and epoch, line 20) a deliberate design distinction or an unintended inconsistency? The source provides no intent statement.", "Are A/B/C/E declared on *Port vs value Port (line 7, 12, 17, 26) intended to have differing semantics, or should all factories share capture-at-invocation behavior? The source does not state intent."], "review_required": true}
